Figure 6 demonstrates that Nano-11 enhances antigen targeting to immunopotentiating cells in the draining lymph node and prolongs antigen retention at the injection site. Panel A shows that MigDCs exhibit the highest expression of the costimulatory molecule CD86 among OVA+ myeloid cells. Panel B further characterizes OVA-positive and negative MigDCs based on CD11b and Ly6C expression. Panel C illustrates that Nano-11, similar to aluminum hydroxide, effectively retains antigen at the injection site for an extended period (up to 7 days) compared to soluble OVA, which rapidly dissipates.